  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "In order to read tutorial prompt better, look around by moving mouse while
    holding [RMB]. Holding [RMB] prevents infuence of crusor position on drone rotation/tilt.\n\nWhen
    operating aerial drone one cannot simply move forward as if using a vehicle.
    Drones are moved/rotated by tilting fans.\n\nWhite circle in the middle of the
    screen designates safe cursor borders. Moving mouse cursor ouside these safe
    corders tilts/rotates drone.\n\nRight now drone position is fixed is place and
    only allowed to rotate around left-right. In order to rotate right, move mouse
    cursor to the right of safe circle. In order to stop rotating counteract rotational
    movement by moving cursor to the left of safe circle.\n\nControl scheme was not
    made to be simple or intuitive. Or good. Or high quality. Or \nFamiliarize yourself
    with aerial inertia. And also... there is something...\nB E H I N D   Y O U."
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
  m_sharedMaterial: {fileID: 2180264, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
